{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Implementation landed in worktree — Option A, gated on per-mutation success\n\n**How per-mutation success is determined (the operator's hard constraint).**\nNew plumbing, not an approximation of the pass exit code:\n\n1. `dispatch_one._update_one_scalar_update` now returns `(result, applied_fields)`.\n   `applied_fields` is assigned on **exactly one line** — immediately after\n   `client.update_issue` returns — so it is unreachable unless that call completed. It\n   stays empty on the parent-only skip and on the 400 illegal-transition arm (which posts a\n   comment INSTEAD of the edit), and every raise propagates past it.\n2. `update_one` forwards it through a `fields_synced` out-param (same shape as the\n   existing `subop_applied`).\n3. `apply_handlers.handle_update` records it onto `BatchApplyContext.synced_fields` keyed\n   by local_id, at a site that sits **past every soft-fail return** (404, assignee-unresolved),\n   and the `record_backstop_failure` path never reaches it at all. Two independent gates.\n4. `applier.apply`/`_apply_batch` copy it out through a `synced_fields_out` out-param;\n   `reconcile._apply_mutations` forwards it only when the resolved applier accepts the kwarg\n   (an un-introspectable signature counts as NO — a false positive would TypeError the pass).\n5. `_advance_baselines` writes the fetch via `set_baseline`, then overlays the confirmed\n   pushes via the new `peer_state.merge_baseline` (a per-field MERGE, not a whole-dict\n   replace). The overlay also runs for a confirmed binding whose key was **out of the fetch\n   window** — our own write cannot be a missing observation.\n\nDeliberately **all-or-nothing per `update_issue` call**, not per field: that call fans out to\nupdate_priority/transition_issue/workitem-edit, so a late failure can leave an early field\nlanded and we under-report it. Under-reporting only makes the baseline LAG (next pass\nre-pushes); over-reporting would make it LEAD, which does not self-correct.\n\n**RED proof.** Two independent demonstrations:\n* Against unmodified main, replaying the incident inputs through the real\n  `_advance_baselines` + `diff_canonical_fields`: baseline retained `To Do`, canonicalized\n  to `open`, local `open` matched it, `outbound changed = {}` — status suppressed, exactly\n  the observed `changed=[description]` shape.\n* With the fix neutered to pre-fix behaviour (overlay made a no-op, all signatures kept, so\n  the failure is behavioural not a TypeError): **all 5 ABA cells fail**, one per mirrored\n  field, plus the partial-apply and out-of-window cells — 7 failed / 9 passed. The 5\n  held-firm cells and the soft-fail cells stayed GREEN through that neutering, which is the\n  point: they pin behaviour the fix must not change.\n\n**Coverage.** All five mirrored fields (summary/description/priority/status/assignee):\n* `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_baseline_advance_aba_e6e9.py` — ABA oracle x5,\n  held-firm x5, soft-fail, partial-apply, empty-map equivalence, out-of-window, unknown\n  local_id, legacy-store degrade (16 tests).\n* `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_synced_fields_reporting_e6e9.py` — the per-mutation\n  success contract on the real update_one/handle_update against a stub transport: unreachable\n  transition, 400 comment-fallback, 404, parent-only, and the handler seam (8 tests).\n* `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_live_path_direction_preservation_e6e9.py` —\n  closes the coverage gap: ADR 0026's mandated direction-preservation cell existed on the LIVE\n  path for `title` only; the other four were pinned against\n  `adapters/jira/outbound_fields._diff_fields`, which 625b left with **no production caller**.\n  16 cells now drive `outbound_field_diff.diff_canonical_fields` for all five fields, with an\n  explicit reachability assertion (`outbound_differ.compute_update_fields is …` AND\n  `compute_update_fields.__globals__['diff_canonical_fields'] is …`) so they cannot degrade\n  into the 599e / 24f7 'passing by not running' class. Verified at runtime, not assumed.\n\n**Module-size cap.** dispatch_one was 785/800 and reconcile 733; the change pushed both over.\nResolved by moving the baseline-advance cluster (`_advance_baselines`/`_advance_peer_parent`/\n`_accepts_synced_fields_out`) into `reconcile_helpers.py` — the documented home for pure\npass-support helpers with no back-edge to the reconcile_once spine — with re-exports so\n`reconcile._advance_baselines` still resolves for the A3 integration oracle. All touched\nmodules now under the cap (dispatch_one 796, reconcile 716, reconcile_helpers 602).\n\nADR 0026 gains Decisions 5 and 6 recording last-synced semantics and the per-mutation-success\ngate, plus the live-path direction-preservation requirement in Consequences."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786131304484396001,"uuid":"d12605f6-db0f-4ba7-a5b8-29d15e3fbef4"}